---
import { agents } from "../../lib/agents";
import { hookIntegrations } from "../../lib/hooks";
import { agentLogos } from "../../lib/logos";
import SectionHeading from "./section-heading.astro";

const featuredAgentIds = [
  "claude",
  "codex",
  "gemini",
  "copilot",
  "opencode",
  "warp",
  "qwen",
];

// Only agents the CLI still supports and that have a logo are featured.
const featuredAgents = featuredAgentIds.flatMap((id) => {
  const agent = agents.find((a) => a.id === id);
  const logo = agentLogos[id];
  return agent && logo ? [{ ...agent, logo }] : [];
});

const hookNames = new Intl.ListFormat("en", {
  style: "long",
  type: "conjunction",
}).format(hookIntegrations.map((hook) => hook.name));
---

<section aria-labelledby="hp-agents" class="border-border border-b">
  <div class="hp-frame mx-auto max-w-7xl border-border border-x">
    <SectionHeading
      id="hp-agents"
      title="Wired into the agent loop, start to finish"
    >
      Your agent learns the standard before it writes, gets checked after every
      edit, and takes over whatever autofix can’t settle. Nothing waits for CI.
    </SectionHeading>
    <ol
      class="grid gap-px border-border border-t bg-border bg-clip-padding md:grid-cols-2"
      role="list"
    >
      <li class="flex min-w-0 flex-col bg-background">
        <div
          class="flex h-72 min-w-0 flex-col justify-center gap-3 border-border border-b bg-muted/60 p-4 sm:p-8"
        >
          <div
            class="min-w-0 rounded-md bg-panel p-4 font-mono text-[12.5px]/6 text-panel-foreground ring-1 ring-black/20"
          >
            <p class="truncate">
              <span class="text-signal">$</span> npx skills add haydenbleasel/ultracite
            </p>
          </div>
          <div
            class="min-w-0 overflow-hidden rounded-md bg-code p-4 font-mono text-[12.5px]/6 text-muted-foreground ring-1 ring-foreground/10"
          >
            <p class="text-foreground">skills/ultracite/SKILL.md</p>
            <p class="mt-1 line-clamp-3">
              <span class="text-foreground">description:</span> Ultracite is a zero-config
              linting and formatting preset for JavaScript/TypeScript projects. Use
              when setting up Ultracite, running check, fix or doctor, writing code
              that follows its standards, or troubleshooting.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 p-6 sm:p-8">
          <p class="font-mono text-accent text-xs/5 uppercase tracking-wider">
            1 · Setup
          </p>
          <h3 class="font-medium text-xl/7 tracking-[-0.015em]">
            Let your agent install it
          </h3>
          <p class="max-w-[48ch] text-pretty text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">
            Add the Ultracite skill and ask for it. Your agent learns how to run <code
              class="font-mono text-sm">init</code
            >, <code class="font-mono text-sm">check</code>, <code
              class="font-mono text-sm">fix</code
            > and <code class="font-mono text-sm">doctor</code>, and how to
            troubleshoot the result.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="flex min-w-0 flex-col bg-background">
        <div
          class="flex h-72 min-w-0 flex-col justify-center gap-4 border-border border-b bg-muted/60 p-4 sm:p-8"
        >
          <div
            class="min-w-0 overflow-hidden rounded-md bg-code p-4 font-mono text-[12.5px]/6 text-muted-foreground ring-1 ring-foreground/10"
          >
            <p class="text-foreground"># Ultracite Code Standards</p>
            <p class="mt-1 truncate">
              - Prefer <span class="text-foreground">`unknown`</span> over <span
                class="text-foreground">`any`</span
              > when the type is genuinely unknown
            </p>
            <p class="truncate">
              - Specify all dependencies in hook dependency arrays correctly
            </p>
            <p class="truncate">- Provide meaningful alt text for images</p>
          </div>
          <ul class="flex items-center" role="list">
            {
              featuredAgents.map((agent, index) => (
                <li class:list={["-mr-1.5", index > 5 && "max-sm:hidden"]}>
                  <img
                    alt={agent.name}
                    class="size-9 rounded-lg ring-2 ring-muted"
                    height="36"
                    src={agent.logo}
                    title={agent.name}
                    width="36"
                  />
                </li>
              ))
            }
            <li class="ml-4 font-mono text-muted-foreground text-xs/5">
              {agents.length} agents
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 p-6 sm:p-8">
          <p class="font-mono text-accent text-xs/5 uppercase tracking-wider">
            2 · Before it writes
          </p>
          <h3 class="font-medium text-xl/7 tracking-[-0.015em]">
            The standard, in your agent’s context
          </h3>
          <p class="max-w-[48ch] text-pretty text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">
            <code class="font-mono text-sm">init</code> writes the rules into
            AGENTS.md, which all {agents.length} agents read, so generated code
            starts close to passing.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="flex min-w-0 flex-col bg-background">
        <div
          class="flex h-72 min-w-0 flex-col justify-center border-border border-b bg-muted/60 p-4 sm:p-8"
        >
          <div
            class="min-w-0 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-code ring-1 ring-foreground/10"
          >
            <p
              class="border-border border-b px-4 py-2 font-mono text-muted-foreground text-xs/5"
            >
              .claude/settings.json
            </p>
            <pre
              class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-[12px]/[1.6] text-muted-foreground">{`{
  `}<span class="text-foreground">"hooks"</span>{`: {
    `}<span class="text-foreground">"PostToolUse"</span>{`: [
      {
        `}<span class="text-foreground">"hooks"</span>{`: [{ `}<span class="text-foreground">"command"</span>{`: `}<span class="text-accent">"bun run fix --hook"</span>{`, `}<span class="text-foreground">"type"</span>{`: "command" }],
        `}<span class="text-foreground">"matcher"</span>{`: "Write|Edit"
      }
    ]
  }
}`}</pre>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 p-6 sm:p-8">
          <p class="font-mono text-accent text-xs/5 uppercase tracking-wider">
            3 · After every edit
          </p>
          <h3 class="font-medium text-xl/7 tracking-[-0.015em]">
            Hooks that check each file it touches
          </h3>
          <p class="max-w-[48ch] text-pretty text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">
            A hook fixes every file your agent edits in {hookNames}. In Claude
            Code, CodeBuddy, Windsurf, and Copilot in VS Code, it hands what it
            can’t fix back to the agent.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="flex min-w-0 flex-col bg-background">
        <div
          class="flex h-72 min-w-0 flex-col justify-center border-border border-b bg-muted/60 p-4 sm:p-8"
        >
          <div
            class="min-w-0 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-panel p-4 ring-1 ring-black/20"
          >
            <pre
              class="font-mono text-[12.5px]/[1.65] text-panel-foreground"><span class="text-signal">$</span>{` npx ultracite fix --codex
`}<span class="text-panel-muted">┌</span>{`  ultracite fix — powered by Codex
`}<span class="text-ok">◇</span>{`  Autofix complete. 9 issues in 3 files left for Codex.
`}<span class="text-ok">✓</span>{` `}<span class="text-panel-muted">src/queue.ts:2:22</span>{`  no-async-promise-executor
`}<span class="text-ok">✓</span>{` `}<span class="text-panel-muted">src/queue.ts:23:26</span>{`  require-await
`}<span class="text-signal">⠋</span>{` `}<span class="text-panel-muted">src/config-loader.ts:3:10</span>{`  no-eval
`}<span class="text-signal">⠋</span>{` `}<span class="text-panel-muted">src/config-loader.ts:10:22</span>{`  eqeqeq`}</pre>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 p-6 sm:p-8">
          <p class="font-mono text-accent text-xs/5 uppercase tracking-wider">
            4 · When autofix can’t
          </p>
          <h3 class="font-medium text-xl/7 tracking-[-0.015em]">
            Your agent CLI fixes the rest
          </h3>
          <p class="max-w-[48ch] text-pretty text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">
            <code class="font-mono text-sm">ultracite fix --claude</code> or <code
              class="font-mono text-sm">--codex</code
            > sends what’s left to Claude Code or Codex, which repairs the codebase
            file by file with edit-only permissions.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
